      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "We aimed to define the role of treatment using statins (3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl coenzyme A reductase inhibitors) in the management of patients with carotid artery disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "LITERATURE SEARCH METHODS",
          "content": "We searched PubMed for studies evaluating the effect of statins on carotid IMT and the occurrence of cerebrovascular events."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "LITERATURE SEARCH RESULTS",
          "content": "Current evidence indicates that routine statin therapy reduces carotid intima-media thickness progression and stroke risk. Additionally, statin treatment significantly reduces perioperative as well as long-term morbidity and mortality in patients undergoing carotid surgery or endovascular interventions. It would also be expected that statins would reduce coronary events in this high-risk population."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Statins should be considered as an essential component of the therapeutic approach of patients with carotid artery stenosis."
        }
      ]},
